    "description": "HMAC, short for Hash-based Message Authentication Code, is a mechanism for message authentication using cryptographic hash functions. It combines a secret key with the message to produce a fixed-size digest, providing both data integrity and authenticity.\n\nHMAC is defined in RFC 2104 and is widely used in API authentication, JWT signatures, and webhook verification.\n\nHMAC is computed with ``hash_hmac()``, which accepts a hashing algorithm, the message, and a secret key.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    $key     = 'secret-key';\n    $message = 'important data';\n    \n    $hmac = hash_hmac('sha256', $message, $key);\n    \n    echo $hmac; // 64-character hexadecimal string\n\n?>",
